  "definition": "AI-only horizontal strokes with up to five cue-ball cushions, high/low and moderate side tips within the existing cue disk. A 3.2 m/s cue-head exploration cap is an engineering choice within the existing 5 m/s manual limit, not a measured player limit or cue-ball speed. Rear-ball interference, near-rail high-tip access and double-hit exclusions remain. Complexity is a soft cost balanced against next-shot quality and landing-zone stability. No forward physics or manual controls are changed."
